I need to find the measure of the largest interior angle of triangle $ABC$.
Since triangle $ABC$ is isosceles, the two sides that are equal in length are $AB$ and $AC$.
The base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal, so angle $B$ and angle $C$ are both equal to angle $A$.
Therefore, angle $B$ and angle $C$ each measure 20 degrees.
Since triangle $ABC$ is obtuse, one of its angles must be greater than 90 degrees.
Since angle $A$ is 20 degrees, the largest interior angle must be either angle $B$ or angle $C$.
Therefore, the measure of the largest interior angle of triangle $ABC$ is $\boxed{80}$ degrees.

