Next, we can use the Shoelace formula to calculate the area of the polygon. The Shoelace formula is given by:

Area = 1/2 * |(x1y2 + x2y3 + ... + xn-1yn + xny1) - (y1x2 + y2x3 + ... + ynx1)|

Using the coordinates of the vertices, we can plug them into the formula:

